AB  - Using data from over 42,000 respondents to the 2022 Strategic National Arts Alumni Project (SNAAP), this study examines how artistic and community-engaged work predict satisfaction with social contribution and value alignment. Results from regression analyses indicate that both arts-related occupations and community-engaged responsibilities are significant positive predictors of these outcomes, even after controlling for demographics. Findings highlight artistic work as a form of civic labor and support protean and boundaryless career models emphasizing self-directed meaning and societal contribution.
