TY  - CPAPER
AU  - Cannon, M
ED  - Muller, VC
TI  - An Enactive Approach to Value Alignment in Artificial Intelligence: A Matter of Relevance
T2  - PHILOSOPHY AND THEORY OF ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE 2021
LA  - English
CP  - Philosophy and Theory of Artificial Intelligence (PT-AI)
AB  - The Value Alignment Problem in AI research is the challenge of how to "align the values" of AI with those of humans such that, as AI systems develop, they do not become an "existential risk" to humans. A fundamental feature of how the problem is currently understood is that AI systems do not take the same things to be relevant as humans do, for example, eradicating the human species in order to "solve climate change". Conceived in this way, the Value Alignment problem is "how do we make relevant to AI what is relevant to humans?" Existing approaches do not address this feature. This paper offers an approach, inspired by Enactive and "4E" cognition, which is oriented toward engaging the Alignment Problem in this way. Naturally, there are benefits and challenges.
