KW  - SCHEME
KW  - SECURE
AB  - Promoting electronic certificates (e-certificates) is an important convenience measure to realize the high efficiency and intelligence of digital government services. This study develops a research model based on behavioral reasoning theory (BRT) and regulatory focus theory (RFT) to understand the public's application behavior of e-certificates, thus expanding the empirical exploration of government service from the perspective of audience psychological motivation. A two-stage mixed-method approach is used: the first phase involved qualitative interviews to determine reasons for and against applying for e-certificates; the second phase comprised a quantitative study with 496 valid samples using PLS-SEM to examine the model. Results show that value alignment impacts the reasons for and against applying for e-certificates, as well as the intention to apply. Reasoning also affects behavior and intention to apply. Additionally, regulatory focus plays an important moderating role in the relationship between reasoning and application behavior. These conclusions offer practical strategies and recommendations for governments and policymakers.
