TI  - Techno-optimism and the Enhanced Games: a critical analysis of medically supervised radical human enhancement
T2  - JOURNAL OF THE PHILOSOPHY OF SPORT
LA  - English
KW  - Enhanced Games
KW  - doping
KW  - techno-optimism
KW  - performance enhancement
KW  - athlete welfare
KW  - value alignment
KW  - FAIR PLAY
KW  - SPORT
KW  - SPIRIT
KW  - WORLD
AB  - This paper critically analyses the Enhanced Games (EG), a 2026 sporting event embracing medically supervised enhancement, techno-optimism and venture-capital funding. Focusing on the EG's four pillars - science, safety, compensation and funding - the authors show how the project aligns with core values in the philosophy of sport, including athlete welfare, fair play and excellence. They argue that the EG are best understood not merely as a challenge to anti-doping policy but as part of a broader transhumanist project of human enhancement. While the EG expose inconsistencies in anti-doping governance and may catalyse a new sporting equilibrium, they risk reducing sport to a spectacle of biochemical superiority. Initial results also suggest that enhancement may enable athletes to regain and surpass previous performance levels despite age and years of stagnation.
