TI  - Developing Effective and Value-Aligned AI Tools for Journalists: 12 Critical Questions to Reflect upon
T2  - JOURNALISM PRACTICE
LA  - English
KW  - Journalistic AI
KW  - generative AI
KW  - investigative journalism
KW  - computational journalism
KW  - document classification
KW  - machine learning
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is playing an increasingly prominent role in journalism, with emerging tools like large language models (LLMs) and other AI applications gaining traction. This paper explores the current landscape in adopting AI tools for the information gathering and story development phase in journalistic practice. We identify two contemporary challenges for implementing AI tools in journalism: effectiveness and value alignment. While the first challenge includes the issues of generalizability, costs, user-friendliness, and accuracy, the latter refers to adherence to journalistic values, independence from external actors, transparency, and data privacy issues. We reflect upon these challenges based on the development process of prototyping an open-access AI tool for classifying documents and prioritizing information-rich pages in collaboration with the Organized Crime and Corruption Reporting Project (OCCRP), a globally recognized investigative journalism network. Based on the literature and our experience, we derive twelve critical questions that we deem important to guide the development of future AI tools for journalism.
