TI  - Nonzero Ue3 and TeV leptogenesis through A4 symmetry breaking
T2  - PHYSICAL REVIEW D
LA  - English
KW  - DISCRETE SYMMETRY
KW  - NEUTRINO MASS
KW  - CP-VIOLATION
KW  - BARYOGENESIS
KW  - MATTER
KW  - WMAP
AB  - We consider an effective theory with an SU(2) x U(1) x A(4) x Z(2) x Z(4) symmetry and investigate the possibility of a linking TeV-leptogenesis with a reactor angle vertical bar U-e3 vertical bar through A(4) symmetry breaking which is at a scale higher than electroweak scale under the framework of radiative seesaw. It has been shown that tribimaximal (TBM) mixing can be obtained by forging vacuum expectation value alignment of the A(4). Especially, one A(4) triplet scalar field with cutoff scale Lambda is added in neutrino Yukawa sector, which is responsible for the deviation of the exact TBM, to explain leptogenesis as well as a nonzero vertical bar U-e3 vertical bar. Above the scale of Lambda the leptonic Yukawa sectors will lead to the exact TBM. We analyze possible spectrums of light neutrinos and their flavor mixing angles corresponding to heavy Majorana neutrino mass ordering, and show that nonresonance leptogenesis at TeV scale constrained by low energy data is achievable, both analytically as well as numerically. We show that only normal hierarchical spectrum of light neutrino would be strongly favored by the current Wilkinson Microwave Anisotropy Probe data, and also show that a relatively large vertical bar U-e3 vertical bar corresponds to the value of baryon asymmetry 6.2 x 10(-10).
